    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d345">

                <pb facs="0432" n="260" sameAs="frus:frus1917Supp01v01/pg260"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 763.72119/568</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Argentina</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Stimson</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary
                        of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Buenos Aires</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1917-04-20T12:00:00-04:16">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">April 20, 1917, noon</hi></date>. <lb/> [<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Received 2.30 p.m.</hi>]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Your April 19, 5 p.m. The proposed congress of American nations to be called upon
                    the initiative of Argentina to meet at Buenos Aires was first called peace
                    congress (see my February 27, 11 a.m., and March 3, 11 a.m.<anchor n="1"
                        xml:id="d345-f1"/>), then called only a commercial congress (see my March 3,
                        noon,<anchor n="2" xml:id="d345-f2"/> your March 14, 6 p.m., my March 16, 6
                    p.m., and my April 16, noon<anchor n="3" xml:id="d345-f3"/>), and now called
                    officially Congress of the Nations of America (see my April 17, 1 p.m.<anchor
                        n="4" xml:id="d345-f4"/>). All of these telegrams refer to the same
                    subject.</p>
                <p>The idea has been accepted so far by Bolivia, Brazil, Chile, Colombia, Cuba,
                    Mexico, Paraguay, and Peru but the invitations are not yet issued.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Stimson</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
